  "notes": [
    "Call seed-specific transfer supported if seed1-minus-seed0 12k point is positive and seed1 upper CI includes zero; call it clear only if the difference CI excludes zero. Downgrade the current 12k bounded-residual route if both seed point estimates are below -11.4275 and the pooled 10k upper CI is also below -11.4275. Do not treat a pooled average over different policies as a benchmark qualification result.",
    "The 10,000-hand pooled-policy average combines two different frozen policies and is research-level seed-distribution evidence only; it is not a benchmark result for one policy."
  ],
  "result": {
    "summary": "Exact seed1 12k completed eight fresh625 sessions at -11.11 bb/100 CI[-49.879,+27.659], seats -17.971/-4.227, with all 15,404 decisions audited. Seed1-minus-seed0 12k was +43.42 CI[-10.929,+97.769]; seat0 difference was +66.074 CI[+2.492,+129.657]. The average across two different 12k policies was -32.82 CI[-59.997,-5.643]. Full suite: 241 passed.",
    "conclusion": "External transfer is highly training-seed sensitive. Seed1 is directionally at the Standard10 reference and both seats pass the preregistered breadth floor, while seed0 was far worse. The between-seed overall difference narrowly crosses zero, so stable learned improvement is not established; nevertheless seed1 satisfies the preregistered criterion for a 20k same-policy confirmation.",
    "decision": "ADMIT_SEED1_12K_FRESH20K_CONFIRMATION",
    "next_step": "Freeze bundle SHA 21b08229 and base SHA 91b0c587 unchanged and run eight new 2,500-hand greedy journaled sessions. Combine no hands with this pilot for the primary confirmation; report the new 20k raw result independently, then decide whether seed1 merits larger training/evaluation or whether seed sensitivity requires objective redesign."
  },
